  "title": "COP31 Climate Talks in Turkey: Deep Division Over Fossil Fuels and Climate Agreement",
  "summary": "The COP31 climate talks in Turkey collapsed as countries failed to agree on a climate deal, with key delegates expressing concerns about the lack of mention of fossil fuels. The talks, scheduled to end Friday, faced strong condemnation for not including fossil fuels in the draft document.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "EU, UK and allies in the developing world rejected what they called an unacceptable deal on the future of the climate, which failed even to mention fossil fuels",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The proposed deal 'failed to meet the moment', said Ireland’s environment minister, Darragh O’Brien, speaking for the EU. 'We will not endorse a decision that does not respond to the science and that actually risks deepening the chasm between global commitments and the action required. [It] does not even mention fossil fuels.'",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The talks, which had become the longest in summit history, to fall apart. The first such failure since 2009.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
